        ],
        "description": "Christiansen Hall of Music is a home of the Music Department and part of the Music Organizations staff that supports concerts and tours by the ensembles. Named after St. Olaf choir founder F. Melius Christiansen, the building houses Urness Recital Hall, the Margaret Skoglund Reception Room, the Halvorson Music Library, three ensemble rehearsal rooms, classrooms, practice rooms, faculty studios, and the electronic music studio. Related Links Music Department Christmas Festival",
