          }
        ],
        "description": "Built in 1877, Old Main was the first - and originally the only - building to occupy Manitou Heights, containing classrooms, a library, housing for students and faculty, and a dining room. Through the years, Old Main has housed various departments in the humanities and now is home to the Religion Department. The hill to the east of the building is a popular sledding venue for students and local neighbors.",
        "floors": [],
        "name": "Old Main",
        "nickname": "OM",
