            "label": "Special Collections"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Completed in 1942 and named in honor of 1905 alumnus Ole Rolvaag, former St. Olaf professor of Norwegian and author of Giants in the Earth, Rolvaag Library is the largest of three libraries on the St. Olaf campus (the others are the Hustad Science Library in Regents Hall and then Halvorson Music Library in Christiansen Hall of Music). Special Collections and College Archives are located on the second floor of Rolvaag Memorial Library. The Halvorson Music Library is located in the Christiansen Hall of Music. The fourth floor of Rolvaag is home to the Information Technology (IT) Department and the Digital Scholarship Center (DiSCO), which provides the campus community assistance with technology and digital scholarship. The English Department and classrooms are located on the fifth floor of the library in the original section of the building. Related Links College Archives Digital Scholarship Center (DiSCO) English Department Information Technology (IT) Hong Kierkegaard Library - The Hong Kierkegaard Library is now located in Steensland Hall Information Technology (IT) Helpdesk Norwegian American Historical Association (NAHA) Special Collections",
        "floors": [],
        "name": "Rolvaag Memorial Library",
        "nickname": "RML",
        "offices": [],
        "abbreviation": "RML",
