        "description": "With such features as a green roof, aggressive daylighting, and the minimization of chemical and biological waste, LEED Platinum-certified Regents Hall is not simply a model for responsible environmental stewardship, but a daily working example of sustainability in practice. Since opening in fall 2008, the building - along with the adjacent Regents Hall of Mathematical Sciences - has become an invaluable teaching tool for nearly 40 percent of St. Olaf students who pursue a major or concentration in the natural sciences or mathematics. Related Links Biology Biomolecular Science Chemistry Environmental Studies Mathematical Biology Natural Lands Neuroscience Nursing Physics Psychology",
