        "description": "Tomson Hall opened in 2011 after an extensive renovation of the 1960s-era Science Center. The building is named in honor of O. Jay Tomson '58 and his wife, Patricia McCarthy Tomson '59. Tomson houses a number of academic departments and administrative offices. Academic Departments Asian Conversations Asian Studies Classics Education French German Languages Across the Curriculum Norwegian Nordic Studies Russian Spanish Administrative Offices Admissions Business Office Academic Success Center Dean of Studies Financial Aid Institute for Freedom and Community (IFC) The Smith Center - International Studies and Global Engagement The Piper Center Office of the President Provost and Dean of the College Registrar's Office Residence Life Fun fact: The movie A Serious Man was filmed in this building in 2008, just prior to its renovation.",
        "floors": [],
        "name": "Tomson Hall",
